    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλωπ-ιστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who adorns himself, dandy</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόκαλος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				1.27
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1401b24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.Herc.</u>
				1457
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>9.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλωπ-ιστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλυντήριος</span>
			, c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.23.14
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the art of
			embellishment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.766
			</span></i>.</div>
